{"raw": {"https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39644": {"title": "Job Details", "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Criminology Position # F00220 Department Sociology and Criminology Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/26/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Sociology and Criminology at Arkansas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Criminology position beginning in Fall 2027. A Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related field is required; applicants nearing completion of the doctorate (ABD) may be considered. Area of specialization is open, although the ability to teach courses within the program\u2019s core requirements will be given priority. The ability and willingness to teach in both in-person and online formats is preferred. Duties & Responsibilities: Regular responsibilities include teaching, research, advising and mentoring students, as well as engaging in service at the university, disciplinary, and community levels. The standard teaching load at Arkansas State is 12 credit hours per semester, but there is commonly a semester course release provided for research for pre-tenure faculty. Teaching assignments will include undergraduate courses in criminology and may include graduate-level courses. The successful candidate will teach core courses consistent with program needs while also\u00a0teaching\u00a0courses in their areas of expertise and interest. About Arkansas State University and the Department Arkansas State University is a comprehensive R2 public research university located in Jonesboro, Arkansas, approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to more than 300 majors in its BA programs in Criminology and Sociology. The department offers a B.A. in Criminology in both traditional and fully online formats, as well as a B.A. in Sociology and an M.A. in Sociology. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Minimum Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a related field is required for this position; applications nearing completion of the doctorate (ABD) may be considered Applications should include the following: a) cover letter describing teaching and research interests b) curriculum vitae c) evidence of teaching effectiveness d) unofficial transcripts e) contact information of three references E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39667": {"title": "Job Details", "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences & Risk Management Position # F00496 Department Health Sciences and Risk Management Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/31/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Arkansas State University Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Health Sciences & Risk Management (tenure-track) to begin in Fall 2027. The position is full-time (9-month) and tenure-track. Duties & Responsibilities: The primary teaching assignment and research focus will be in the Department\u2019s Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management Program. The ideal candidate will demonstrate potential for an active, high impact emergency management research program. Responsibilities include producing peer-reviewed publications, presenting at professional conferences, and applying for external funding. Additional responsibilities include preparing, developing, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across multiple programs in the Department of Health Sciences and Risk Management. Applicants should have the ability to teach a broad range of courses across disciplines such as emergency management, health and/or public administration, policy, research methods, and program development and evaluation. Faculty are expected to maintain regular office hours, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and participate in course/program assessment. Faculty are also expected to engage in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities that are in the best interest of the students, university, community, and the discipline at large. The ideal candidate will contribute to the development, assessment, and advancement of academic programs, including curriculum development, program assessment, workforce alignment, and engagement with external stakeholders. Arkansas State University is a public research university located in Jonesboro, AR. Arkansas State University is designated by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education as a \u201cResearch 2: High Research Spending and Doctorate Production\u201d institution. The Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management has a multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary focus across its programs in Disaster Preparedness & Emergency Management, Dietetics/Nutritional Science, Public Health, Occupational & Environmental Safety & Health, and Health Studies. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: \u2022 Strong computer/technology skills required, or possess the ability to easily obtain needed skills. (Microsoft Office, Blackboard Learn and/or Canvas, variety of WEB based programs, etc.) \u2022 Strong written and verbal communication skills required. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit their (1) curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of purpose indicating research interests and teaching philosophy, (3) a writing sample (recent peer-reviewed article or dissertation chapter), and (4) contact information for three academic references, that can speak to your research and teaching, that will be contacted if chosen for an interview. All materials should be submitted online via Taleo, and all items must be submitted to be considered. Application review will begin on the closing date in Taleo and will continue until the position is filled. Questions can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Amy Hyman, at ahyman@astate.edu. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. or terminal research degree in an emergency management or closely related discipline. Candidates who are ABD will also be considered, provided they obtain their degree by July 1, 2027. Candidates should have a strong research agenda in the emergency management discipline, or a closely related discipline with an emergency management focus, with evidence of peer-reviewed publications and/or external funding, or the potential to quickly develop a strong research agenda and be immediately successful regarding research and in obtaining external funding. Candidates should also have experience with face-to-face and online teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39692": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page This job has moved or is no longer available. Please search our current job openings ."}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39143": {"title": "Job Details", "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Director of DVM Programmatic Outcomes Position # F00731 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/15/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Director of DVM Programmatic Outcomes supports the College of Veterinary Medicine\u2019s Office of Professional Education in evaluating student achievement of program outcomes and supports CVM faculty in development of curricular assessments. Duties & Responsibilities: Contribute to development of curricular assessment activities (e.g., objective structured clinical examinations, written assessments, workplace-based assessments) and \u00a0document evidence of student learning and progress throughout the curriculum. Supervise administration of standardized national exams. Support faculty in educational activities by providing consultations (ie regarding assessment construction or analytics), providing faculty development seminars and resources in \u00a0assessment, advising courses and curriculum Provide statistical support for educational research or educational scholarly work Oversee administration and analysis of curricular and student outcomes (student surveys, course evaluations, faculty, graduating seniors, and alumni) Contribute to accreditation reports Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: \u2022 Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff. \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders. \u2022 Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. Required Documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references. Minimum Qualifications: An earned Master\u2019s degree. PhD preferred. One year of experience with outcomes assessment. An equivalent combination of years of experience and education may be considered for substitution of educational requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39635": {"title": "Job Details", "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Instructor Position # F00713 Department Engineering Instruction Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Engineering Management at Arkansas State University invites applications for the full-time tenure-track position of Instructor. Duties & Responsibilities: Position located in Jonesboro, AR. Responsibilities include the following: Teach graduate and undergraduate level in-class and online courses in engineering management as well as related engineering courses as needed. Assist in developing new courses, curriculum, and evaluation tools. Advise and mentor students, serve on various committees, and administer comprehensive finals and projects. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Other: Minimum Qualifications: The position requires the following: Master's Degree in Engineering Management or a related field. For full consideration, applicants must apply for position number F00713 at https://www.astate.edu/jobs/. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39741": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Dance and Choreography 9 Mo Position # F00266 Department Theatre Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/9/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Theatre at Arkansas State University invites applications for a Full-Time Assistant Professor of Theatre in Dance and Choreography. This is a 9-month tenure-track teaching appointment starting Fall 2027. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be responsible for: Teaching a 4/4 load, which typically includes three academic courses and one production course (directing/choreographing). Other possible courses include, but are not limited to, Theatre Appreciation, Ballet, Musical Theatre Dance, Jazz Dance, Tap Dance, Folk and other Dance courses as determined by the faculty member\u2019s area(s) of specialty and expertise. Maintaining an active record of research and/or creative activity Overseeing the Stage Manager for shows when directing. Attending evening/weekend rehearsals as appropriate Mentoring and supervising student choreographers and dance captains. Being available for student supervision during evening and weekend rehearsals and performances Working collegially and collaboratively with students and faculty. Department Overview: The Arkansas State University Department of Theatre offers rigorous theatre training in a liberal arts environment. Students receive a comprehensive education, whether choosing a general approach or the more select experiences within the three emphases: Acting, Design and Technology, or Musical Theatre. The curriculum is designed to combine classroom instruction with practical production experience, as both are integral to the student\u2019s development. Classroom experiences provide theoretical, historical, and critical examinations of the theatre as art, craft, and discipline, while production experiences offer practical opportunities for exploring and applying these concepts. This liberal arts-based education provides opportunities to master critical thinking, communication, and creative problem-solving skills, preparing graduates to become engaged, thoughtful, and compassionate citizens of a global world. Facilities: The Department of Theatre is housed within Fowler Center, Arkansas State University\u2019s premier performing arts complex. The 344-seat Drama Theatre serves as the primary venue for plays and musicals, featuring stepped seating to maximize sight lines and acoustics designed for spoken drama productions. The proscenium features a 40\u2019 x 20\u2019 opening, and a complete catwalk system provides access for lighting and rigging areas. The stage house features a suspended floor and full fly-loft, rigged so that scenic properties may be \u201cflown\u201d out of view. Adjacent to the Drama Theatre is the Simpson Theatre, a flexible black box space that allows for various configurations, providing students opportunities to develop skills required to work in many different kinds of venues. Additional facilities include a Light Lab equipped with intelligent LED theatrical lighting and a small theatrical sound system, a Design Lab featuring Apple iMacs with CAD, lighting and sound design software, and access to Adobe\u2019s Creative Cloud, as well as drafting tables and a wide-format printer. The Costume Shop is equipped with 14 Bernina sewing machines, industrial irons, sergers, a dye vat, cutting tables, and an embroidery machine. The Scene Shop is among the finest in the region, equipped with a variety of professional-grade stationary and portable power tools, as well as a 3D printer. About Arkansas State University: Arkansas State University (A-State), founded in 1909, is the second largest university in Arkansas and serves over 15,000 students. As a Carnegie Research 2 institution and the premier university of the mid-South, A-State is committed to teaching, research, and service. Located in Jonesboro, A-State offers a vibrant campus life with a diverse student body and a strong tradition of student-focused instruction. With more than 150 degree programs, including robust online offerings, A-State combines world-class research with academic excellence and is a catalyst for progress in the Delta and Mid-South region. About Jonesboro: Jonesboro is the regional hub of Northeast Arkansas for healthcare, entertainment, business and industry. It is the 5th largest city in Arkansas with a population of over 76,000. The Metropolitan Statistical Area (MSA) encompasses over 130,000 people. The A\u0002State campus is centrally located in Jonesboro with the thriving downtown entertainment sector to the west and the growing Hilltop area to the east. Jonesboro provides convenient access to major markets via interstate and four-lane highways. Memphis, TN (1 hour), Little Rock, AR (2 hours), St. Louis, MO (4 hours), and Nashville, TN (4 hours). Additional Considerations: Experience directing theatrical productions. Experience teaching Theatre for non-majors. Experience teaching ballet or other foundational dance techniques. Membership in professional organizations such as SETC, ACDA, or MTEA. Other Teaching Areas of Expertise: Stage Combat, Movement for Actors, Yoga, Non-Western Dance Techniques Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Applicant should present evidence of excellence in teaching, active scholarly and creative work, knowledge of current trends in the field, and artistic leadership in the areas of theatrical dance and choreography. General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM plus additional hours for production(s) on weekdays, weekends and evenings. Other: Application deadline: Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applications for position F00266 must be received online. This position is housed on the Jonesboro campus. Visit https://jobs.astate.edu for detailed information and to apply for the position. Please upload the following: \u25aa Cover letter addressing qualifications \u25aa Curriculum vitae \u25aa Indication of professional dance and/or choreography work, such as a portfolio, performance reel, or documentation of creative work. \u25aa Contact information for five professional references Transcripts will be requested by the search committee after initial screening of applicants. For additional information, please contact: DayDay Robinson, Assistant Professor of Theatre. Email: drobinson@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: \u25aa M.F.A. in Theatre, Dance, or a closely related field, or equivalent professional experience. \u25aa Demonstrated proficiency in teaching both dance and choreography for theatrical productions. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39759": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Political Science Position # F00286 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the level of assistant professor, beginning in Fall 2027. The search is open with respect to subfield and substantive focus within political science. We seek a colleague with an active, publishable research agenda who will contribute to the department's growing research profile and its graduate programs (an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA). Because our curricular needs span the discipline, we are especially interested in candidates prepared to teach across more than one area, including political institutions, state and local government, international relations, and research methods. The teaching load is consistent with the department's research expectations. Duties & Responsibilities: The teaching load is consistent with those at research-oriented institutions and with the department\u2019s expectations for research productivity. Faculty workload includes research, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Faculty members deliver instruction, carry out research, perform service for their respective professions and community, and participate in the management of the University through shared governance. Each member of the faculty has the duty to deliver instruction and maintain a learning environment consistent with the highest standards of the profession. The faculty has a responsibility to set degree requirements, assess when they are met, and establish and maintain curricula that meet professional standards and fulfill the educational goals of the University. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date All items listed below are requirements must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete: (1) A statement of purpose indicating research and teaching interests (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) a writing sample (e.g., recent peer-reviewed article, book chapter, or dissertation chapter) (4) three letters of recommendation Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 100 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs\u2014an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program. The latter includes an enrollment of more than 150 students Questions can be directed to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: PhD in political science or a cognate field. ABD candidates will be considered, but the doctorate must be completed by the start date of the appointment. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39792": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Public Administration Position # F00192 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the level of assistant professor in public administration, beginning in Fall 2027. The search is open with respect to area of specialization within public administration and public policy, and comparative perspectives are welcome. We seek a colleague with an active, publishable research agenda who will contribute to the department's growing research profile and to its NASPAA-accredited MPA program, where the primary teaching responsibility will lie. Because our curricular needs in the MPA program span the field, we are especially interested in candidates prepared to teach across more than one area, including some combination of public management, leadership, grant writing, and human resources management. The successful candidate will also occasionally contribute to the department's undergraduate offerings in political science. The teaching load is consistent with the department's research expectations. Duties & Responsibilities: The teaching load of the faculty is in alignment with a Carnegie-classified R2 research institution. Faculty workload includes research, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Faculty members deliver instruction, carry out research, perform service for their respective professions and community, and participate in the management of the University through shared governance. Each member of the faculty has the duty to deliver instruction and maintain a learning environment consistent with the highest standards of the profession. The faculty has a responsibility to set degree requirements, assess when they are met, and establish and maintain curricula that meet professional standards and fulfill the educational goals of the University. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date All items listed below are required and must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete: (1) A statement of purpose indicating research and teaching interests (2) Curriculum Vitae (3) A writing sample (e.g., recent peer-reviewed article, book chapter, or dissertation chapter) (4) Three letters of recommendation, to be requested if selected for interview. Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 120 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs\u2014an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program, the latter with an enrollment of more than 230 students. Questions can be directed to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: PhD in public administration, public policy, political science, or a cognate field. ABD candidates will be considered, but the doctorate must be completed by the start date of the appointment. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39749": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 9 Month Working Title Online Instructor of Public Administration Position # F00582 Department Government-Law-Policy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/19/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Government, Law & Policy at Arkansas State University, a Carnegie-classified R2 research university, invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position in public administration, beginning in Fall 2027. This is a fully online teaching position, and the successful candidate may work remotely. The primary teaching responsibility will be in the department's NASPAA-accredited online MPA program, with the potential to also teach public administration and policy courses in the department's online undergraduate program in political science. The search is open with respect to area of specialization within public administration and public policy. Because our online curricular needs span the field, we are especially interested in candidates with flexible teaching interests who are prepared to teach across more than one area, including some combination of public management, leadership, budgeting and finance, grant writing, human resources management, and non-profit management. Candidates with substantial applied experience in public or nonprofit organizations are encouraged to apply, as are candidates with a demonstrated record of effective online instruction. Duties & Responsibilities: The primary responsibility of this position is the delivery of high-quality online instruction in the MPA program and, as needed, the online undergraduate program in political science. Although all faculty are expected to mentor students, the primary focus of this position is teaching courses and contributing to the ongoing success of the MPA program. Other duties as assigned. All items listed below are required and must be submitted in order for your file to be considered complete : A statement of purpose indicating teaching interests and relevant professional experience Curriculum Vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., sample syllabi, student evaluations, or a brief teaching statement addressing online instruction) Three letters of recommendation, to be requested if selected for interview. Arkansas State University is a comprehensive public research university located approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis, TN. The department offers a well-rounded curriculum to its more than 120 majors. The department also offers two graduate programs\u2014an MA in Political Science and a NASPAA-accredited MPA program, the latter with an enrollment of more than 230 students. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma. This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in-person engagement as needed. The primarily online teaching modality means that some flexibility may be needed in work schedules to accommodate student needs. Applicants wishing to work in person will be provided with a full faculty office and resources should that be preferred. Questions can be sent to cwimpy@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: An earned MPA or a related master's degree with substantial professional experience in public or nonprofit management is required. PhD, DPA, or other terminal degree in public administration, public policy, political science, or a cognate field is preferred. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38795": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 12 Mo Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Small Animal Urgent Care Position # F00722 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/29/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a clinical assistant or associate professor in Small Animal Urgent Care. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position incorporates clinical work (24 weeks/year) with workplace-based year 4 student training in urgent care/emergency, teaching of year 1-3 students in clinical skills and urgent/emergency care. Service (10%) is also expected. Scholarly activity appointment is negotiable. Duties & Responsibilities: Teach year 1-3 DVM students the principles and practice of urgent care and emergency medicine in the classroom, clinical skills laboratory Teach year 4 DVM students urgent care and emergency medicine in clinical practice Provide excellent patient care and clinical service, including communication with clients and referring veterinarians Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on small animal emergency medicine and urgent care across years 1-4 of the DVM curriculum Contribute to objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs) and other skills-based assessments Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Mentor and advise DVM students +/- Contribute to scholarly endeavors through collaborative educational research and/or educational innovations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: \u2022 Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff. \u2022 Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders. \u2022 Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently. General Days/Hours: Variable hours (approximately 4 pm-12 am when on clinical duty, M-Th, ~24 weeks per year; 8 am-5 pm M-F when not on clinic duty) Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required Documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 DVM or equivalent \u2022 Board certification in a small animal specialty (preferred) (e.g., ACVECC) \u2022 Two (2) years of teaching experience (preferred) \u2022 Experience in competency-based veterinary education (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38557": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty 12 Mo Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Small Animal Practice Position # F00486 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/29/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a faculty position in Small Animal Practice. This will be a 12-month, full time, non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This will be a predominantly teaching position (85% teaching) and include research/scholarly activities and service. Teaching of DVM students will be in a competency-based veterinary curriculum incorporating lecture, lab and small group learning. Duties & Responsibilities: Teach small animal clinical and surgical skills and communication and professionalism to DVM students using models, simulations, specimens, and live animals in years 1-4, in laboratory sessions, small and large group classroom sessions Work with other clinical and professional skills veterinarians and staff Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on small animal professional, clinical and surgical skills across years 1-4 of the DVM curriculum Contribute to development of assessments in communication, professionalism, and clinical skills, including objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs) Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Contribute to scholarly endeavors through collaborative educational research and/or educational innovations Contribute to classroom instruction of DVM students (large and small group) Responsibilities may include clinical practice if desired Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note that all position postings close at 12:00 am CST on the position closing date. The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Two years of teaching experience (preferred) \u2022 Experience in competency-based veterinary education (preferred) Required Documents \u2022 Cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: An earned Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent is required for this position. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39835": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor of Special Education Position # F00642 Department School of Teacher Education Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/17/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Educational Leadership, Curriculum and Special Education (ELCSE) of the College of Education and Behavioral Science is seeking applicants for a 9-month, non-tenure track Temporary Instructor of Special Education position. Candidates will teach in an online Special Education Program, which may include initial and advanced programs in special education K-12. The successful candidate will be a strong collaborator and have a desire to connect with colleagues and build relationships to ensure a strong program. The successful candidate will have experience in developing and teaching special education and curriculum courses, mentoring students, and being involved in appropriate activities for the maintenance and continuous improvement of the program. Candidates are expected to be well-versed in behavior management, characteristics of exceptional learners, special education law and ethics, educational assessment, the Science of Reading, and experience in supervising field activities Duties & Responsibilities: Instruction and course development in special education. Teach 15 hours in special education and/or a variety of areas at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Develop and modify courses as needed Work with a team of academic assistants to support the courses the candidate designs Work collaboratively with faculty in the special education program and other department programs Provide supervision for field experiences Serve on program, department, and university committees Participate in program, department, college, and university-level meetings Carry out other functions as may be appropriate to the position Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: \u2022 Candidates will preferably demonstrate successful teaching experience at the master's and specialist levels; have experience with online teaching, Canvas LMS, and be proficient in utilizing and incorporating technology into instruction and research efforts. \u2022 Knowledge/experience regarding literacy and assessment (specifically Science of Reading, and the use of High-Quality Instructional Materials). General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Classroom teaching experience (a minimum of three years) in P-12 public schools in Special Education \u2022 Teaching experience in higher education \u2022 Teaching experience in on-line teaching Minimum Qualifications: An earned Master's degree in Special Education or in a related field of education E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39876": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant/Associate Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychology Position # F00338 Department Psychology & Counseling Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/23/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Psychology and Counseling at Arkansas State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychology. Preferred expertise in Coding & Data Driven Research, but we will also consider other areas of expertise depending on evolving needs of the department. Position to begin August 2027. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities may include classes such as statistics and research methods. Depending on the background and interest of the candidate, other courses within our curriculum will also be available (e.g., Developmental, Cognitive, Social, etc.). We also welcome the development of new classes within the coding and data theme as well as new classes in the candidate\u2019s specific specialty area. Faculty have the opportunity to work with and mentor students as part of their research labs. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Approximately 8 faculty are in the core undergraduate BS Psychology degree program, and there are many opportunities for collaboration within the program with faculty who have a wide range of specializations. The department also houses counseling and school psychology programs, and cross-program collaboration often takes place. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Arkansas State University is a comprehensive, state-supported, doctoral university with high research activity (R2). Jonesboro is a community of over 70,000 people located in northeast Arkansas. We are an hour\u2019s drive from Memphis, Tennessee. Jonesboro boasts a regional center for quality healthcare, a variety of dining and entertainment options, a low cost of living, and plenty of recreational opportunities. Arkansas State University does not discriminate on the basis of color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, race, age, national origin, religion, marital status, veteran status, genetic information or disability in any of its practices, policies or procedures. This includes, but is not limited to, employment, admissions, educational services, programs or activities which it operates or financial aid Questions regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Jessica Curtis, curtis@astate.edu Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of research experience and plans, a reference list with at least three individuals, and a statement of teaching philosophy to the electronic application Minimum Qualifications: A doctoral degree in Psychology or a related field is required. Candidates who are advanced ABDs will be considered at the rank of instructor until the dissertation is defended. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39860": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor in Animal Science Position # F00114 Department Agricultural Studies Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/23/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The College of Agriculture, Arkansas State University-Jonesboro, invites applications for a nine-month appointment as a tenure-track assistant professor with an anticipated start date of August 2027. We are seeking an outstanding individual with expertise in the area of animal or poultry science. The nine-month appointment is in support of academic programs, scholarly activities, and service. The successful applicant will have a strong commitment to: teaching and student learning assessment at all university levels; development of an impactful applied research program; and university/community service. Duties & Responsibilities: Normal teaching load is 12 credit hours with an option for an applied research (25%) component release Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in any of the following areas: meat science, poultry science, animal production, animal genetics, animal physiology, and animal behavior and welfare The successful candidate will develop an applied research program in their area of expertise, secure extramural funding, mentor thesis\u2013level graduate students, and publish results in high-quality scientific journals Service and leadership activities with professional societies are encouraged, while service on departmental, college, and/or university committees is required The faculty member will have undergraduate recruiting and retention responsibilities for students in the Animal Science major Possibilities exist for summer salary support through summer teaching, research collaborations, and extramural funding The office of Research and Technology Transfer is available to assist with grant applications and other extramural funding opportunities Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Applicants must have demonstrated: interest and desire to interact with the regional agriculture community, and potential for high-quality teaching, applied research, and scholarship. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m. Regular and reliable attendance Additional hours as requested and/or needed Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. In addition to collaborative opportunities with colleagues within the College of Agriculture, A-State College of Agriculture faculty have the opportunity to collaborate with regional producers and scientists at other agricultural research institutions. These include area livestock and poultry producers as well as faculty in the A-State College of Veterinary Medicine, College of Sciences and Mathematics, the Arkansas Biosciences Institute, and the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture. Preferred Qualifications: \u2212 Teaching experience in both lecture and laboratory settings \u2212 Expertise in regionally relevant livestock and poultry production \u2212 Involvement in collaborative research settings \u2212 A track record of grant writing and journal publication success \u2212 Involvement working with FFA/4-H and collegiate student organizations Minimum Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in Animal Science, or D.V.M. with teaching and/or research experience, or a closely related field. Candidates near degree completion of the Ph.D. (ABD) may be considered Applicants must have expertise in the areas of livestock or poultry production and management, animal genetics, and animal physiology. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39867": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Agricultural Economics Position # F00189 Department Agricultural Studies Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/23/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Assistant Professor of Agricultural Economics; full-time, nine-month, tenure-track appointment with a starting date in August 2027. The appointment is to support the academic programs, scholarship, and service/outreach missions of the college. Duties & Responsibilities: The initial nine-month appointment is primarily a teaching position (75%) with an applied research component (25%) focusing on agribusiness. Specific responsibilities include: Teach primarily undergraduate agribusiness courses and some master's level graduate courses. Participate in curriculum and course development, recruit and mentor students, supervise student interns, advise student organizations, and provide service through college and university activities. Establish relationships with public and private organizations. Opportunities exist for collaboration with crop and livestock producers, agricultural input and credit suppliers, commodity handlers and food manufacturers, agribusiness trade associations, and government agencies. Develop applied research and outreach programs in agribusiness. Opportunities for collaboration outside the college exist with faculty in the A-State College of Business, the USDA-ARS Delta Water Management Research Unit, and the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Applicants must have an excellent ability to speak and write the English language, strong interpersonal skills, the potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching, and the ability and desire to interact and collaborate with the agribusiness community. Review of applications will begin after the position closing date. Candidates will be notified by phone or email once the position has been filled. General Days/Hours: Monday \u2013 Friday 8:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: A-State, the flagship campus of the Arkansas State University System, is in Jonesboro, Arkansas. Jonesboro is the educational, medical, industrial, and agriculture hub of northeast Arkansas. The region features extensive and intensive crop and animal production and is the location of several food manufacturing facilities. Minimum Qualifications: The A-State College of Agriculture seeks an individual with an earned Ph.D. in agricultural economics, agribusiness, or a closely related field. A.B.D. applicants near degree completion will be considered. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39868": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Department Chairperson Working Title Department Chairperson Position # F00005 Department History Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 12/21/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department Chair needs to be motivating, organized, and supportive. The Chair leads and manages departmental faculty and staff. They are responsible to their respective Dean for the general management and operation of their academic areas. The Chair represents the department to the Dean and university administrators, supports faculty in their scholarship and professional development, and works with faculty to improve instructional programs and to develop programs that are responsive to the changing needs of students. Some administrative experience at Chair, Assistant Chair, or Program Director is preferred, though applicants meeting minimum qualifications will be considered. Duties & Responsibilities: Evaluating and recommending faculty members to the Dean of their college for employment, retention, promotion, tenure, non-renewal, and dismissal Encouraging and sustaining scholarship, research, grant activity and participation in professional activities by members of faculty in alignment with A-State\u2019s R2 status. Supervising other personnel in the department Preparing and administrating departmental budgets Coordinating curricular development; strategic planning; outreach and recruitment; alumni audience and donor relations; and service activities while demonstrating commitment to excellence in teaching The standard teaching load for department chairs is two courses per academic semester Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Arkansas State University is a comprehensive R2 public university located along Crowley\u2019s Ridge approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis. The History department offers a well-rounded curriculum through the BA in History and the BSE in Social Science, and also offers courses in Geography. The department offers the MA in History on campus and online. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in History. A tenured appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor Required Documentation: CV, cover letter, and a list of 3 - 5 references E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39884": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Department Chairperson Working Title Music Department Chairperson Position # F00013 Department Music Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/1/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University (A-State) is recruiting applicants for the position of Department Chair beginning July 1, 2027. A-State seeks a visionary leader and music educator who will join a music department recognized throughout the region for artistic excellence and student success. Duties & Responsibilities: The Department Chair is responsible to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Communication for the general management and operation of their academic area. The Chair represents their department to the Dean and university administrators, assigns faculty load, supports faculty in their professional development, and works with faculty to constantly improve instruction and develop programs that are responsive to the changing needs of students. The duties of this position will consist of half-time administrative load release and half-time teaching load in the individual\u2019s area of expertise or as needed by the department. The Department Chair plays a particularly important role in encouraging and sustaining performance, scholarship, research, service, and participation in professional activities by members of the faculty. They also supervise and hire other personnel in the department including non-classified staff and adjunct faculty. The Department Chair duties include: Assigning teaching loads and classes for faculty and staff Evaluating and recommending faculty members to the Dean of the College of Liberal and Communication for employment, retention, promotion, tenure, non-renewal, and dismissal Supervising student recruitment, retention, and success Managing records, budgets, and financial accounting Overseeing the maintenance of the Department of Music website, social media, advertising, and music student/faculty handbooks Submitting requests to Facilities Management for supplies and building maintenance as needed The successful candidate will: Advocate for the needs of the Department of Music through compelling data, metrics, and narratives Leverage strong musical and administrative skills to unify, recruit, and retain exceptional faculty talent Provide evidence of strong musicianship through performance and/or scholarship Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: General Days/Hours: The Department Chair will be expected to have regular and reliable attendance Monday-Friday during the school day (8am-5pm) to teach courses, hold office hours, and participate fully in departmental, collegiate, and university activities. Additional hours outside of the school day are expected as needed for items that include but are not limited to concerts, recruiting, and outreach. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin 11/1/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please note that all position postings close at 12:00 am CST on the morning of the position closing date. Applications for this position must be received online at http://www.astate.edu/jobs. Select employment opportunities and choose the Department Chair (F00013) position to apply. Materials: Applicants should upload a 1) cover letter addressing qualifications, 2) curriculum vitae including names and contact information for five professional references, 3) three original letters of reference, 4) statement of administrative philosophy (2-3 pages), 5) statement and/or documentation of scholarly/creative activity, 6) unofficial copies of all collegiate transcripts. Recruitment Information Comments: Load: 6 hours administrative and 6 hours teaching/service; SCH is variable. The majority of our current DoM faculty team are instructors and pre-tenure faculty and all of our eligible tenured faculty have full and specialized loads. Located in Jonesboro, AR, a growing city of 80,000 residents, A-State maintains a reputation for high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs as well as a strong commitment to the community and region. As a prominent cultural hub in the Mid-South, the A-State Department of Music serves over 300 students, has a comprehensive offering of undergraduate and graduate degrees, a wide range of instrumental and vocal performance groups, a generous scholarship program for music and non-music majors, and a talented and committed faculty that wants to help their students reach their personal and professional goals. Our talented faculty and students showcase their hard work and musical ability on the Riceland Hall stage in the beautiful Fowler Center, in the newly renovated Recital Hall in the Fine Arts Center, on Allison Field at Centennial Bank Stadium, and in other performing arts spaces across Jonesboro and beyond. A-State is committed to building and sustaining a culture of academic excellence characterized by teaching, scholarship, creative activity, and service supportive of the acquisition of knowledge, skills, and abilities necessary for personal fulfillment, successful careers, and responsible citizenship in an increasingly diverse and global society. To achieve that goal, background investigations are conducted on all final applicants recommended for employment. Minimum Qualifications: An earned Doctoral degree in music. Special consideration will be given to candidates who have administrative experience and can provide evidence of effective management of faculty and budgets, as well as proof of recruitment and retention in their area of expertise. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39901": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Nursing Position # F00259 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/29/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Nine (9)- month non-tenure-track undergraduate faculty position in the ACEN-accredited A-State School of Nursing. Participation in teaching and professional service is expected. This position is full-time, with a focus on weekend clinical placement in the BSN and AASN program options. Duties & Responsibilities: Actively participates in development and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, and test construction. Responsible for clinical and didactic courses appropriate to areas of expertise. Plans and supervises clinical seminars. Establishes effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies. Continues education for professional growth through continuing education offerings. Participates in student mentoring and guidance. Maintains regular office hours on campus and virtually Participates in appropriate program, college and university activities as assigned for faculty and/or student recruitment and retention Serves on assigned program, college, and university committees. Sponsors and promotes planned activities of students, program, college and university as requested. Contributes to the community through involvement in and/or consultation to health-related organizations, board memberships, or professional presentations to the public Holds membership and participates in organizations that advance the profession of nursing, such as ANA, ARNA, Sigma, or other professional organizations Optional Participation in nursing research and other scholarly work, including but not limited to presentations at professional meetings, publications, grant applications, book and textbook reviews, and enrollment in university courses. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of curriculum design, strategies to promote student learning, assessment and evaluation of learning, evidence-based education principles, basic nursing skills and a commitment to life-long learning. Possesses interpersonal and communication skills necessary to teach as part of a faculty team. Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Primarily weekend coverage, Typically, Thursday - Monday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. (hours vary related to clinical rotations, office hours, didactic course load, and other program activities). Regular and reliable attendance on campus and assigned clinical facility. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Up to 15 credit hour teaching workload. Primary coverage is weekends for online program options for undergraduate nursing, assistance with covering on campus and distant campus program options, as needed Academic experience preferred in the areas of medical/surgical nursing, ICU, mental health, and/or maternal/child. A cover letter, resume, and a list of 3 references must be attached (in MS Word or PDF format) to the electronic application Minimum Qualifications: 1) An Earned Doctorate degree required, PhD preferred, or DNP 2) Unencumbered licensure to practice nursing as an RN in Arkansas or a compact state. 3) At least two (2) years of clinical practice as an RN. 4) Didactic and/or clinical teaching experience in nursing, preferred. *If the degree held is a Masters of Science in Nursing Degree, the position will be at the rank of Instructor. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39909": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Director Working Title Director of Fowler Center Position # A02710 Department Fowler Center Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/31/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University invites nominations and applications for the position of Director of Fowler Center. Fowler Center stands at the center of artistic life at Arkansas State University. Serving students, faculty, artists, and the surrounding region, the center houses theatre productions, concerts, museum exhibitions, guest artists, educational programs, conferences, and community events throughout the year. As the home of the Bradbury Art Museum and multiple performance venues, Fowler Center unites visual art, music, theatre, and public engagement under one roof. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Communication, the Director is responsible for all aspects of building operations and management including event booking, box office, scheduling, staffing, equipment, and property. The Director will have a thorough knowledge and understanding of concepts, principles, and practices of event management; a proven record of booking musical and entertainment talent and academic lectures; and, strong marketing and promotion experience with similar type venues to facilitate fulfillment of A-State\u2019s vision for Fowler Center to be recognized as a premier arts and cultural event center. Duties & Responsibilities: Direct management of all academic and public-facing spaces in Fowler Direct booking of top musical and entertainment talent and academic presentations across a variety of venues Direct marketing initiatives for all events in Fowler Direct staff to provide exceptional customer service for each event Oversee financial management of Fowler by preparing a budget based on goals and monitoring expenditures with financial records. Lead recruitment of all staff positions, including full-time, part-time, and student employment Monitor industry trends and news that will have a local impact on the organization Coordinate with the Department of Theatre, Department of Music, and the Bradbury Art Museum for Fowler scheduling and promotional needs as appropriate Conduct key constituent meetings Promote a facility reputation for outstanding customer service Develop a year-round facility maintenance plan, including discussion of long-term improvements and short-term maintenance, working with Facilities Management to define scope of work and cost estimates. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of concepts, principles and practices of event management Proven record of effective management of a facility comparable to Fowler Center Strong marketing and promotion experience with similar-type venues and a proven track record of growing business and enhancing customer experience Excellent people management skills General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance This position requires the flexibility to work various hours based upon need and may include days, nights, weekends, and holidays Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor\u2019s Degree with an emphasis in Fine Arts, marketing, event management, management, or a related field Senior-level arena or venue management, substantial marketing, or management job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for education E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39976": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Specialist III Working Title Administrative Specialist III Position # A00977 Department University Centers Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Beebe Proposed Salary Range: $30,000.00 Closing: 10/24/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Specialist II is responsible for researching and preparing special reports, examining and verifying documents, and performing general office duties. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Collects, copies and prepares materials and tests for A-State Jonesboro faculty Schedules testing appointments, proctors tests and returns exams by various methods Recruits, hires, schedules, and supervises work-study students. \u00a0Also approves their time in Banner Schedules advising appointments for A-State students with advisors who are coming to our campus to meet with their advisees Assists students with admission and registration processes Assists with recruitment for the A-State degree center.\u00a0 Is the primary contact for students seeking degrees through the degree center in areas outside of nursing and education Provides direction to degree center students who need help navigating the various departments on the Jonesboro campus when seeking information Works with Distance Education at Jonesboro in assigning rooms and produces paper schedules for distribution through the degree center Orders degree center supplies, assists with travel authorizations/expenses as needed, helps degree center coordinator with the budget, etc.\u00a0 (this is a new responsibility as of this year so we aren\u2019t quite sure what all will be involved) Provide reports and information as needed to A-State and ASU personnel. Schedules classes on the A-State-Beebe campus Establish and maintain computerized and paper files Assists A-State students with Wi-Fi and computer access while on the Beebe campus Assists with A-State graduation ceremonies for the degree center Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of record keeping procedures Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics Knowledge of work-related subject area Knowledge of computers and software applications Ability to conduct research and compile data into report form Ability to establish and maintain filing systems Ability to operate standard office equipment Ability to analyze documents to determine compliance with rules, regulations, and procedures Ability to communicate both orally and in writing General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Work closely with all Departments, the Registrar's office and ITS to assist students and the problems that might arise Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma One (1) years of experience in a specialized or related area applicable to work performed E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39983": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Support Supervisor Working Title Administrative Support Supervisor Position # A01020 Department Biological Sciences Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/24/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Support Supervisor is responsible for supervising the activities of support level personnel within an assigned department or program Duties & Responsibilities: Greet incoming individuals and answer the telephone, directing inquiries to the appropriate person. Manage all office correspondence, including all incoming and outgoing mail and e-mail directed to and from the Biological Sciences Department, faculty, and graduate students. Maintain calendar for Chair of Biological Sciences Department. Take notes at faculty meetings. Advertise and schedule departmental events. Coordinate academic and co-curricular activities within the department. Prepare faculty and graduate student phone and e-mail lists. Assist graduate students and direct student inquiries to the appropriate faculty or staff member. Assist with tracking Graduate Student FormStack forms and their progress within their program. Coordinate on-campus interviews of prospective faculty. Concur Travel \u2013 Faculty, Students, and Guests of A-State Work with Department Business Coordinator to make sure budget resources are available. Prepare Travel Authorization through Concur Travel. Use Department Travel Card to make travel reservations (airline, hotel, registration, secure vehicle safety for all drivers using department vehicles or rental cars). Prepare 14-Day Advance travel memo if required. Work with faculty to make travel arrangements for Biology Seminar speakers and faculty candidates as required. Prepare Travel Expense Reports through Concur Travel on behalf of travelers, reallocate charges to appropriate account(s) as necessary. Note: Travel expense reports should be processed within 10 days of return. Track and prepare P-Card report for office and miscellaneous supplies bought for the office of Biological Sciences. Work with Department Business Coordinator if questions arise concerning reallocation budget for charges. Maintain the Department copier; assist faculty with any copier-related issues; and make copies as needed. Maintain a log of all sensitive and non-sensitive documents leaving the department for additional signatures. For example, Volunteer Memorandum of Understanding for Biological Sciences, Travel Memos, Vehicle Safety Program form (VSP). Point person for reserving Department Fleet Vehicles, upkeep of Vehicle Checklist, Tags, Insurance, and Wex Card for Vehicles. Also responsible for initiating the Vehicle Safety Program Form for faculty/graduate students who will be using Department Fleet Vehicles. Responsible for scheduling vehicle maintenance with Facilities/Motor Pool. Process Work Orders as needed on behalf of the department. Update and maintain department website and recruitment pamphlets, degree/major checklists. Liaison with Information & Technology Services for IT issues. Authority for signing and distributing documents from Access and Accommodation Services to the appropriate faculty Maintain department list of majors and teaching assistants. Maintain 11th-day official course enrollment Enter department\u2019s course schedules into Banner/CourseDog Create variable credit research courses for Biology Oversee Registration Error Reports from Registrar\u2019s office Assist students with class overrides per faculty\u2019s requests TA coordination \u2013 collect student schedules for Fall/Spring and coordinate with needed TA slots. Oversee room scheduling for Bio classrooms, including meetings and defenses. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of record keeping procedures, the principles and practices of mathematics and basic data analysis, work-related subject area, computer, and software applications. Ability to plan and organize. Ability to interpret and apply policy and procedures involving Travel, P-Card, and Graduate Student Policies. Ability to conduct research and compile data into report form, establish and maintain filing systems, operate standard office equipment, and ability to research and analyze related work program information. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma. One (1) year of training in Business Management, Business Education, or a related field Three (3) years of experience in specialized or related field applicable to work performed. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39973": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty 12 Mo Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Veterinary Clinical Pathology (Half Time) Position # VET001 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/14/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a 12-month, half time, non-tenure (teaching) track, Assistant or Associate Professor in Veterinary Clinical Pathology. This will be a predominantly teaching position (90% teaching, 10% service). Teaching of DVM students will be in a competency-based veterinary curriculum incorporating lecture, lab and small group learning. Service will include College, University and outside service and may include opportunities for diagnostic service. This position is designated at 0.5 full-time equivalent (FTE), representing 50% of a full-time appointment. Duties & Responsibilities: Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on veterinary clinical pathology Teach diagnostic reasoning in the DVM curriculum in classroom and laboratory settings (+/- clinical settings) Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Mentor DVM students Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Preferred Qualifications: \u00b7 Two years\u2019 experience as a veterinary clinical pathologist \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to provide high-quality teaching at the college or university level \u00b7 Ability to work in a team within an interdisciplinary environment and in collaboration with other faculty members Minimum Qualifications: \u00b7 A DVM (or equivalent) and hold, or be in the process of obtaining, board certification in veterinary clinical pathology (DACVP or equivalent) \u00b7 Hold or obtain a license to practice veterinary medicine in Arkansas Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39924": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of English Position # F00091 Department English and Philosophy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/7/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of English, Philosophy, and World Languages at Arkansas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English specializing in Writing Studies, beginning in Fall 27. We welcome candidates working across rhetoric and composition and related fields, including writing pedagogy, literacy studies, professional and technical writing, digital and multimodal writing, writing across the curriculum, multilingual writing, critical pedagogy, and rhetorical theory. These areas are illustrative rather than exhaustive. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in writing, as well as general education composition courses, including Composition I and Composition II, and maintain an active research agenda. The ability to teach creative writing in poetry is preferred, ideally supported by an MFA in poetry. Candidates without this secondary specialization or credential will receive full consideration. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching load of the faculty is normally twelve hours per semester. A reduced teaching load is provided for pre-tenure faculty. Faculty workload also includes research, creative activity, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Arkansas State University provides a number of benefits, including health insurance and retirement. For a complete list, please view: https://www.astate.edu/a/hr/benefits/ Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: We are seeking a dynamic, qualified colleague with the ability to engage students from diverse backgrounds in the study and practice of English writing; evidence and/or potential for successful teaching; evidence and/or potential for an active research program General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date A-State offers an English major, a Writing Studies minor, and a Master\u2019s of English with an emphasis in composition and rhetoric; the Writing Studies minor and Master\u2019s emphasis in composition and rhetoric are growing in both student interest and class offerings. This program features a highly collaborative environment in which faculty work together to create courses and resources to best suit the needs of the diverse and growing student demographic. Teaching load of faculty is normally four courses per semester. Faculty workload also includes research, creative activity and service. Pre-tenure faculty receive a one-class reassignment for research. Arkansas State University serves approximately 14,000 students. The university is committed to quality teaching, including small class sizes, and well-equipped classrooms. It has the largest library in the Arkansas State University System. Jonesboro is an agricultural and industrial city in northeast Arkansas, about 70 miles from Memphis. Qualified candidates should submit electronically: \u2022 Letter of application (through online portal) \u2022 Curriculum vitae (through online portal) \u2022 Research statement (through online portal) \u2022 Statement of teaching philosophy (through online portal) \u2022 If requested, candidates should arrange to have 3 confidential letters of reference emailed to an address to be provided Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 Ph.D. in English, Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. \u2022 Evidence of effective teaching of college-level writing. \u2022 Evidence of an active scholarly agenda appropriate to the field of specialization. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience teaching creative writing in poetry, preferably with an MFA in poetry. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39995": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences and Risk Management Position # F00352 Department Health Sciences and Risk Management Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/16/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Arkansas State University College of Nursing and Health Professions invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Health Sciences and Risk Management (non-tenure track) to begin in Fall 2027. The position is a full-time (9-month), non-tenure track position. The primary teaching assignment is multidisciplinary across programs in the Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management. Preferred applicants should have the ability to teach across a broad range of disciplines, including courses in nutritional science, health studies public health, and other general healthcare courses within the department. Teaching will be assigned based on the degrees, credentials, and licensures held by candidates, and on the program needs of the programs and department. Duties & Responsibilities: Responsibilities include preparing, developing, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across multiple programs in the Department of Health Sciences and Risk Management, as credentialed and needed. Applicants should have the ability to teach across a broad range of disciplines, including courses in nutritional science, health studies public health, and other general healthcare courses within the department. Teaching will be assigned based on the degrees, credentials, and licensures held by candidates, and on the program needs of the programs and department. Faculty are expected to maintain regular office hours, mentor students, and participate in course/program assessment. Arkansas State University is a public research university located in Jonesboro, AR. Arkansas State University is designated by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education as a \u201cResearch 2: High Research Spending and Doctorate Production\u201d institution. The Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management has a multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary focus across its programs in Disaster Preparedness & Emergency Management, Dietetics/Nutritional Science, Public Health, Occupational & Environmental Safety & Health, and Health Studies. Teaching load is 15 hours (5 courses) per semester. Additional responsibilities include maintaining virtual office hours, developing and recording lectures, writing exams, grading, and participating in course/program assessment. Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit their (1) curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of purpose indicating teaching philosophy, and (3) contact information for three academic references, that can speak to your teaching, that will be contacted if chosen for an interview. All materials should be submitted online via Taleo. Application review will begin on the closing date in Taleo and will continue until the position is filled. Questions can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Deanna Barymon, at dbarymon@astate.edu . Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Strong computer/technology skills required, or possess the ability to easily obtain the needed skills. (Microsoft, Canvas and/or other Learning Management Systems (LMS), variety of WEB based programs, etc. Strong written and verbal communication skills required. General Days/Hours: Regular and reliable attendance. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma). This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in person engagement as needed. This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Arkansas State University is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer committed to excellence through diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a master\u2019s degree in a healthcare related discipline. PhD or professional doctorate in a healthcare discipline strongly preferred. Credentialing/licensure in a healthcare discipline required, e.g., Occupational Therapist (OT), Physical Therapist (PT), Registered Dietitian (RD), etc. Candidates holding a master\u2019s degree at the time of hire will be appointed at the instructor rank. Candidates holding a PhD, terminal degree, or professional doctorate will be appointed at the assistant professor rank. Potential candidates should possess experience in online teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39945": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Department Chairperson Working Title Department Chair of Psychology & Counseling Position # F00019 Department Psychology & Counseling Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/6/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department Chair is responsible to their respective Dean for the general management and operation of their academic areas. The Chair represents their department(s) to the dean and university administrators, supports faculty in their professional development, and works with faculty to improve instructional programs and to develop programs that are responsive to changing needs of students. Duties & Responsibilities: Represents their department(s) to the dean and university administrators Supports faculty in their professional development Works with faculty to improve instructional programs Works with program coordinators in Psychology (BS & BA), School Psychology, Clinical Mental Health Counseling, and School Counseling to understand the needs and support the goals of each program. Works with and supports in recruitment and retention of faculty Works with faculty to develop programs that are responsive to changing needs of students. Supervises faculty, conducts annual evaluations, and recommends tenured and nontenured faculty members to the dean of their college for employment, retention, promotion, tenure, non-renewal, and dismissal For the preparation and administration of budgets for the departments; Evaluates and recommends program offerings to the dean For the supervision of the academic mentoring of students majoring in the department Responsible for the acquisition, use, and care of departmental equipment. Addresses student concerns and academic appeals/grievances Acts as a liaison between faculty and administrators Ensures compliance with university policies Ensures accreditation standards are maintained Promotes the department\u2019s accomplishments and impact Encourages and sustains scholarship, research, and participation in professional activities by members of their faculty Maintains an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline Works with and assists in recruitment and retention of students Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with program coordinators and faculty across the department's research and professional programs, including supporting accreditation processes for the counseling and school psychology programs (CACREP, NASP). General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance 12-month contract Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. Preferred Qualifications: Prior academic leadership experience, such as serving as a program coordinator or director. Experience with program accreditation, program review, or assessment is also valued. Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate in psychology, counseling, or a closely related field. Candidates must have a record of teaching, scholarship, and service that meets the Department of Psychology & Counseling's Promotion, Retention, and Tenure (PRT) criteria for appointment with tenure at the rank of associate or full professor. Must be eligible for graduate faculty status at Arkansas State University. Required Documentation: Cover letter, application, resume, 2 letters of recommendation, 3 reference names other than recommenders, and transcripts. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39992": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Fiscal Support Supervisor Working Title Fiscal Support Supervisor Position # A00766 Department Dean of Liberal Arts Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $40,000.00 Closing: 10/26/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Fiscal Support Supervisor is responsible for supervising the activities of fiscal support personnel within an assigned department or program. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Fiscal support supervisor responsible for all budget and accounting issues across all departments in the college; reviews, verifies, and approves all budget related documents submitted to the budget office Maintains faculty and staff computer inventory Works with three ITS staff assigned to CLAC to collect quotes for purchasing computers Supports ITS staff with maintaining classroom inventory records; initiates process for purchasing computers for all computer labs and classrooms in HSS, Fine Arts, ED/COMM, Fowler, Art Annex Supports all units with Taleo Reviews and verifies all Extra Compensation Forms and EPAFs Facilitates allocation of professional development funds Oversees all Foundation Accounts Prepares budget spreadsheet for graduate assistants for the college Facilitates expenditures of academic capital funds Provides support for departments with AOS revenue sharing accounts Provides budget support and performs other selected fiscal processing duties to support Printing Services Develops reports requested by AAR for the college: Auxiliary/Special Funding Budgets Infrastructure Spending Report Merit Recommendations Summer Instruction requests Off-Budget requests Carry-forward Spending Plans Faculty Reassignment Report Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of staff development and supervision principles. Knowledge of department operations, policies and procedures, applicable laws and regulations. Knowledge of software application programs, database management, and accounting principles. Ability to conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews, resolve operational problems, and prepare required reports. Ability to plan, organize and coordinate activities, resources, and materials associated with the needs of the department or program. Ability to plan and direct the work of others. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a bachelor in general business, business administration, finance, or a related field. Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39999": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Registrar Working Title Graduation Coordinator Position # A01067 Department Records and Registration Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $33,500.00 Closing: 10/24/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Assistant Registrar is responsible for the audit of degree plans, the verification the accuracy of data input into the student academic record, and the implementation of registration processes. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Code and review Intent to Graduate cards Review graduation requirements to clear students for graduation Notify students and departments of graduation requirement problems Work with students and departments to resolve graduation problems Post degrees Provide graduation assistance: Assist with graduation planning and ceremony preparation Print diplomas and replacement diplomas Attend all graduation ceremonies Coordinate the awarding of en route associate degrees Order and track graduation supplies Maintain an up-to-date procedure manual Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of computers and software application programs, database management and basic accounting principles, and registration processes Ability to conduct research and perform basic quantitative quality assurance reviews, plan, organize, and coordinate activities, resources, and materials associated with the needs of the department or program, counsel students and families General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree in business administration or related field and two years of experience in higher education administration Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or parts of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39996": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date HEI Program Coordinator Working Title HEI Program Coordinator Position # A00922 Department Financial Aid and Scholarships Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/21/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The HEI Program Coordinator is responsible for conducting special research studies, analyzing data, preparing statistics, making recommendations based on research findings, and monitoring and coordinating project/program activities. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Gather and compile monthly analysis of department data on incoming calls, surveys, and ID entries. Coordinate plans for financial aid presentations at high school, college, and A-State events; manage all details for events hosted by Financial Aid and Scholarships. Assist director and supervisory staff as requested in creation, proofreading, and editing of documents and publications for the department; assist with research and formatting of information for presentation to intended audiences. Initiate and follow through to completion all procurement, travel, personnel, and budget processing; monitor department expenditures and account balances; provide budget status updates as requested. Maintain department calendar of important dates including financial aid presentations on and off campus, dates from Academic Calendar, Treasurer\u2019s Office, Registrar, and employee out-of-office schedules. Maintain inventory and records on department IT devices and peripherals (office-based and portable) assigned to Financial Aid and Scholarships staff; order and monitor stock of office supplies for staff use. Monitor Finesse call manager application throughout the day to assess call team status and assist with answering phone as needed; assist with department email account monitoring during peak periods and when primary monitors are out. Serve as liaison between Financial Aid and Scholarships department and university departments and outside vendors regarding in-office services (copiers, shredding, IT, office maintenance.) Serve as Office Manager, maintaining a comprehensive understanding of office operations, policies, and procedures to provide guidance, support staff across functional areas, assist with workload management and backlogs, and ensure continuity of operations as needed. Other Duties as Assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of planning, research, and analysis techniques and procedures. Knowledge of department operations, policies, and procedures. Knowledge of applicable laws and regulations. Knowledge of basic accounting principles. Ability to plan and execute systems and organizational analysis and feasibility studies. Ability to conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews. Ability to research, prepare, and present comprehensive written and oral reports. Ability to organize and conduct meetings and workshops. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Prospective students and their families. Current students, high school counselors, faculty and staff on-campus. Able to work with other departments effectively. Knowledge of record-keeping procedures. Ability to conduct research and compile data in report form. Ability to establish and maintain electronic filing and data entry. Ability to communicate with students and parents. Knowledge of general office procedures and office equipment. Experience with Excel, Outlook, Word, PowerPoint and other Microsoft Office products. Excellent communication skills. Familiarity with SCT Banner. Knowledge of basic Mathematics and statistics. Basic knowledge of student financial aid and scholarships. Ability to collect, compile, analyze and record data for spreadsheet use. Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree in public administration, general business, or a related field Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}, "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39605": {"title": "Career Center", "description": "Job Details New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Institutional Services Assistant Working Title Institutional Services Assistant - FNBA Position # A01181 Department Custodial Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $27,040.00 Closing: 10/20/26 Please note: All\u00a0postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the\u00a0closing date.\u00a0 This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, class rooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, resident halls, dining areas, building common areas, and other areas as required. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Adhere to the vision and guiding principles of the Finance and Administration Division, which are Fairness, Honesty, Respect and Accountability Perform custodial work assignments and other general work assignments in a professional and courteous manner Working Supervisor is responsible for coordinating the work assignments for their assigned team Motivate, train and interact with the individuals under your supervision to assure assigned work areas are cleaned, maintained and organized on a daily basis Ensure assigned team members are trained to properly use chemicals, supplies and equipment as well as to put in force this use on a consistent bias Maintain an accurate inventory of building supplies and process a requisition to replenish supplies when needed Maintain records regarding maintenance needs and safety deficiencies in assigned areas Request and conduct safety procedural training for members of your assigned team Inspects assigned work areas to ensure the correct level of cleanliness is maintained and correct areas that fail to meet the expected cleaning standard Generate work orders for building and equipment maintenance and other areas of need Develop computer skills in Banner System, FAMIS, and internet usage Empties waste baskets, dumps trash, and replaces trash bags Use cleaning supplies, equipment cleansers and other agents to clean floors, furniture, walls, windows, and windowsills Sweeps, mops, and buffs floors, vacuums and shampoos rugs, cleans baseboards, dusts furniture and fixtures, washes windows and blinds, and empties trash Strips and waxes floors, as needed Cleans bathroom fixtures and stocks bathroom with soap, toilet tissue, and paper towels Collects and launders dirty linens, towels and other soiled items Monitor maintenance and grounds needs and assure that proper reporting procedures are followed Reports work orders to operational personnel concerning minor and major maintenance repairs Conducts inventory of equipment, linens, supplies, and materials to maintain current demands and determine future needs Follow oral and/or written instructions while work independently without close supervision Wear the assigned uniform as designated in the uniform policy Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of basic cleaning techniques and cleaning equipment operation and maintenance Ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work, use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture, use housekeeping cleaning supplies and equipment, work independently without close supervision, follow oral and/or written instructions, perform multiple tasks and to prioritize assignments, perform repetitive manual work, and do required lifting (up to 50 lbs.) General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 6:00 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel with Facilities Management Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma Preferred to possess a valid Driver's License E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"}}, "rows": {"https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39644": {"school_id": 41, "posting_url": "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequis